PROJECT SCOPE
This is a fresh project being built from scratch for this course. I am not reusing code or assets
from previous projects.
The project scope is designed to be achievable for a solo developer within the semester
timeline. The simplified physics approach is specifically chosen to be network-friendly and easier
to debug. The small player count (2-4) keeps the networking manageable. The top-down
perspective simplifies rendering and camera work. The arena boundaries naturally limit the
world size.
By focusing on getting the core gameplay loop working well and stable, then adding networking,
and finally polishing with mitigation techniques, the project follows a logical progression that
matches the course structure.
WHY THIS GAME IS A GOOD CHOICE
• The simplified physics approach provides the fun "weight" feeling without complex code
• Small player count (2-4) is realistic for debugging and testing alone
